# Prompt pack — modify screen `{{screen-id}}`  (tool: {{stitch|claude}})

> The agent fills the {{…}} from the manifest, shows you this to refine, saves it
> under design/prompts/, then either calls the tool (Stitch) or hands it to you
> to paste (Claude Design).

## 1. Prompt to paste into the design tool
```
You are extending an existing product's design system. Read DESIGN.md (and the
codebase) for the current tokens and components — REUSE them, do not invent new
styles.

Screen to modify: "{{screen-id}}"  ← title the artifact exactly this.
Current purpose: {{purpose}}
Change requested: {{the specific change}}
Use only these tokens/components: {{relevant subset}}
Keep unchanged: {{what must NOT change}}
Acceptance criteria: {{bullet list}}
Render light + dark, mobile + desktop.
```

## 2. What to do in the tool
- {{stitch: nothing — the agent runs this via MCP and shows you the render}}
- {{claude: iterate on the canvas until it meets the criteria}}

## 3. What to hand back
- {{stitch: nothing — the agent fetches the screen image + code by id}}
- {{claude: Export → "Hand off to Claude Code" (or download the bundle) and bring
   it here. The bundle may include every screen; the agent will apply ONLY
   `{{screen-id}}` (matched by title + verified by diff) and skip the rest.}}
